g pattern now because  this child was in full-time behavioral  therapy we were actually able to capture  data on self-injurious behaviors as well  over the course of these two weeks and  this basically led us to observe the  trifecta of behavioral exacerbations  gastrointestinal symptoms and an altered  gut microbiome looking more closely at  the specific ASD microbiome we again saw  many bacteria previously reported in ASD  including Clostridium LTA and multiple  other clost realities that we observed  in the ASD cohort of the microsil  microbiome study that I just discussed  these organisms were also absent or  significantly decreased in the sibling  as well as in the unrelated neurotypical  controls so one unexpected finding was  the detection of Hamas parainfluenza  generally a respiratory pathogen but we  previously reported this organ is  in children with irritable bowel  syndrome however in this longitudinal  case study Hamas was interestingly  spikes during both of the GI episodes  with a more pronounced appearance in the  diarrhea episode and actually in the  diarrhea specimen we definitely confirm  the absence of any typical bacterial or  viral pathogen during those TGIF SOT I  running it through a clinical diagnostic  diagnostic GI panel and will continue to  evaluate the potential role of Halawa or  potentially other organisms during each  of those two gastrointestinal events  finally we've also performed global  metabolomic profiling on these samples  and have a multitude of interesting  findings that we're still working our  way through for example you see here  whom arginine appears to spike the  morning of the first GI episode but you  chiral glycine spikes later in the day  at the onset of the dire real episode we  also saw consistent decreases and  several fatty acids and the ASD samples  compared to the neurotypical controls  and neurotypical sibling that our work  continues in creating a comprehensive  data set for the exploration of the gut  mic